	"changes": {
		"body": {
			"from": "Workspace proposal refreshes decrypted every cached mail body when any proposal had a source. This layer selects account-scoped conversation membership from summaries and hydrates only the union of related messages in one coherent SQLite WAL snapshot. Fingerprints, ordering, source-change warnings and synchronous approval/execution checks retain their contracts.\n\nRelated #37. Stacked on #40; sole implementation/delivery owner @pekth. No settings migration, encryption/key change, provider operation, dependency or release change.\n\nValidation:\n\n- 1,153 bounded serial tests passed, including the complete inherited UI stack; 23 focused conversation/store/workspace checks passed.\n- Matched synthetic workload: 3,000 cached messages and one related source decoded 3,000 bodies before, one after. Elapsed 22.2 seconds to 20ms; CPU 20.5 seconds to 29ms; reported peak heap 528.4MB to 47.2MB. This measures one workload, not every native memory spike.\n- Strict TypeScript/Vite build passed.\n- Independent read-only source review found no concrete issue in the complete layer.\n- Exact macOS arm64 package/ad-hoc signature and isolated encrypted startup passed; normal candidate launch was confirmed before commit.\n\nNative long-running CPU/RAM behavior and physical UI acceptance remain separate. The draft status retains the parent stack's native rich-input acceptance hold. No merge or release is requested.\n"
		}
	},
